      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You may not be able to safely diagnose this yourself, but the combination of a sudden severe headache with one-sided weakness and blurry vision is **not typical** for a standard migraine and requires immediate medical attention. Please call emergency services or go to an emergency room right now, as these symptoms could indicate a stroke or a transient ischemic attack (TIA). Do not wait to see if it passes, as every minute counts for your safety. Your emergency responders know these critical warning signs better than any online message can convey.",
