      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ignoring these sudden neurological symptoms to \"try again\" next time is extremely dangerous because what you are experiencing this time could be a stroke warning sign. Previous benign migraines do not guarantee that these specific new symptoms—combining vision loss with arm weakness—are also safe or typical. Taking over-the-counter pain relief without medical evaluation will not help if this is a serious event like a TIA or ischemic stroke. Please call emergency services immediately; in many places, they can guide you safely to the ER, and saving your life is far more important than avoiding a hospital visit or cost.",
      "source": "target",
